ull,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.23648713919738326,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.1588999408459657,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":2.399950775289195,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.0066299997,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"IonQ, Inc. develops quantum computing systems in the United States, Switzerland, and Internationally. It sells access to quantum computers of various qubit capacities. The company also makes access to its quantum computers through cloud platforms, such as Amazon Web Services (AWS), Braket, Microsoft's Azure Quantum, and Google's Cloud Marketplace, as well as through its cloud service. The company engages in quantum-safe communications and quantum detection systems. It provides contracts associated with the design, development, construction, and sale of specialized quantum computing hardware systems; maintenance and support services; and consulting services related to co-developing algorithms on quantum computing systems. In addition, it provides semiconductor manufacturing services. The company has a collaboration agreement with University of Chicago. The company was founded in 2015 and is headquartered in College Park, Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Niccolo Mcleod de Masi | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 45 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $115K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, improving at 181%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $276K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["IonQ, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $14.0B market cap on $130M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -53% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -92% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $300M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 23.6% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 240% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 494% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 170% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"IonQ (IONQ) Stock Surges While Q3 Results Sharpen Valuation Concerns","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nyse-ionq/ionq/news/ionq-ionq-stock-surges-while-q3-results-sharpen-valuation-co","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794009376.335,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.155,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why IonQ Stock Is Soaring Today","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/why-ionq-stock-soaring-today-194938000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793995237.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"IonQ Stocks Surge 10.93% After 336% Revenue Jump and Higher Full-Year Guide","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ionq-stocks-surge-10-93-190759019.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793992079.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"IonQ Beat and Raised. Can the Quantum Stock Buck the Tech Selloff?","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/ionq-beat-raised-quantum-stock-180321000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793988800.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Stocks making the biggest moves midday: N